Z||000007||West Coast Fiero||12-28-2001||11:04 PM||||those 4 parts were the beginning ( upper and intermidiate plenum, and the valve covers. Next step is to remove the trans and replace with another that will be polished and every steel part in the engine bay ( brackets, water neck, decklid hinges, etc... ) will be chromed. The intakes were stripped of all paint, smoothed out to get rid of casting seems, and then pollished, folowed by a clear coat.<P> The bar going across the bay is the strut tower brace made here in house.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
